  "programme": "A native wildflower meadow: drifts of wild bergamot, blanketflower, goldenrod, fireweed, wild blue flax, prairie crocus, prairie smoke, pasture sage, cinquefoil and wild rose among rough fescue, blue grama, feather reed grass and june grass, with massed low blooms in drifts; a winding stone-dust walk to a gathering circle with benches; a mown grass loop; three bee hotels facing the morning sun; four interpretive lecterns; saskatoon, chokecherry and aspen at the edges.",
  "design_basis": "Original concept after the catalogue pollinator meadow \"Wildflower Walk\" references (variant 1). Species are prairie natives from the shared plant library; the mix is a teaching value, not a planting plan.",
